1. Introduction
The Campus Management System is a menu-driven console application intended to bring student administration, course enrollment, academic results, and library operations into a single software system.It demonstrates core C++17 and DSA concepts using persistent text files.
2. Problem Statement
Educational organizations handle student profiles, course registrations, marks, book inventories, and loans.
A scattered/manual approach can cause duplicated enrollment, inconsistent inventory, and difficulty producing reports.
This project provides controlled operations and basic integrity rules.
