7. Data Model and Relationships
Student: Has a unique student ID and profile fields.
Course: Has a unique course ID and an enrollment vector of student IDs.
Result: Associates student ID and course ID with marks and grade.
Book: Tracks total and available copies.
Loan: Connects student and book with issue, due, and return dates and status.
Course and Student are related many-to-many through course enrollment IDs.
8. Data Structures Selection
1. Vector: Convenient collection traversal and dynamic resizing. Deletion may shift later elements.
2. Unordered Map: Used for ID-to-index lookups, with average O(1) complexity.
3. Queue: Used for FIFO waiting requests when a book is unavailable (in-memory only).
4. Stack: Used for session recent-action history.
5. Priority Queue: Used to surface the highest marks first for ranking.
Each structure is used where its access pattern is suitable.
9. Algorithms
Merge Sort
Merge Sort is implemented for student-name sorting. It divides the vector recursively and merges sorted halves.
Binary Search
Binary Search is implemented for student ID lookup only after sorting students by ID using the same ascending comparison.
Priority Queue
Priority Queue provides descending marks retrieval.
Linear Search
Linear scans are used for some relationship and active-loan checks.
