11.11. Grade Policy
The application follows the following grading system:
Marks Grade
90–100 O
80–89.99 A+
70–79.99 A
60–69.99 B
50–59.99 C
40–49.99 D
0–39.99 F
The application validates marks between 0 and 100.
Ranking output orders recorded course results by marks. Equal marks naturally share the same score, but rank numbering policy is not currently implemented as a formal competition rank.
12. File Handling and Integrity
Data files are pipe-delimited.
User-provided pipes and newline characters are sanitized to spaces.
The application:
Loads files at startup.
Saves relevant module files after mutations.
Provides Save All and Exit.
Advances IDs beyond the highest loaded ID.
Rejects duplicate enrollments and capacity excess.
Requires valid enrollment before entering marks.
Blocks student removal when the student has enrollment associations or an active loan.
Ignores malformed rows during loading.
Text-file storage is not transactional, and backup/recovery is a future enhancement.
